  "term": "trisomy 18",
  "definition": "Trisomy 18 is a genetic syndrome caused by an extra full copy of chromosome 18. It is marked by severe physical abnormalities, major intellectual impairment, and a life expectancy that usually does not extend beyond infancy.",
